# Maro won't go down. How hard do you push?
@id maro_floor3
@title Floor Three
@trigger floor_unlocked 3
@order 40

== start
pip (happy): Floor THREE is open! Maro! You've been to Floor Three, right? What's it like?
maro (neutral): Loud.
pip (surprised): That's it?
maro (sad): Dark. Teeth. A crown made of spoons.
? flag heard_spoons -> spoons
-> choice

== spoons
pip (surprised): Sir Bramblewick said someone named Rook—
maro (angry): Bramblewick talks too much.

== choice
* "Maro. What happened down there?"
  -> push
* "You don't have to go back. We've got this."
  ~ affinity maro +1
  ~ bonus cook_speed +0.05
  ~ flag protected_maro
  maro (sad): …
  maro (happy): Hm. Then there'll be hot soup when you get back. Every time.
  -> end
* "Pip — maybe wait before Floor Three."
  ~ flag pip_waits
  pip (angry): Wait?! I've been waiting my WHOLE LIFE.
  maro (neutral): Listen to the boss.
  pip (sad): …Fine. But only until Gerald's cousins are scared of me.
  -> end

== push
? affinity maro >= 2 -> opens
maro (angry): Some other night.
narrator: He turns back to the stove. The conversation is over.
-> end

== opens
~ flag maro_opened
maro (sad): Twenty years ago. Four of us. Odessa, Wren, me — and Rook.
pip (surprised): Wren?! My MUM was in your crew?
maro (sad): The rats came up the stairs like water. Rook stood his ground and told me to run.
maro (sad): I ran. I've been running ever since. Up here, where the soup is.
pip (sad): …
maro (neutral): Bring everyone home, Pip. That's all I ask.
-> end
